use /lib
from /scope/open-projects import OpenProjectsScope
from /ui/components/history-list import HistoryListScope

export shape MessageListScrollingShape:
    description:
        The latest task's table scrolls with its lock to the bottom off to
        start with, until switched on. Each open project keeps how far its
        latest task's table was scrolled and whether it was locked, and the
        rest of its message list as it was left, as the @{OpenProjectsScope}
        says, so switching back to it shows the list just as it was.

        However long the list of previous tasks grows, drawing it costs no more
        than drawing the tasks in view, so scrolling, animations, and new output
        stay smooth.

    scrollingPast:
        Scrolling carries on past either end of the latest task and the
        previous tasks, from one to the other, but only on purpose: a scroll
        that reaches an end stops there, however hard it was flung, and only
        a new scroll, begun after the scrolling has come to rest at that end,
        goes on past it.

        With the latest task's output scrolled to its top, a new scroll up
        expands the previous tasks, as clicking their row does, opening
        scrolled to the bottom, on the tasks sent most recently, as the
        @{HistoryListScope} says. Before any task has been sent, or with no previous
        tasks, scrolling up does nothing more.

        With the previous tasks expanded and scrolled to their bottom, a new
        scroll down closes them, as clicking "Back to the latest task" does,
        bringing back the latest task and its output, scrolled to its top.

        A scroll carried on in the same motion, such as a fling's momentum
        still running when an end is reached, never crosses over. Output or a
        list too short to scroll is always at both its ends, so any new scroll
        over it that leads somewhere crosses over. Only the wheel or trackpad
        crosses over. Scrolling sideways, dragging a scrollbar to an end, and
        scrolling anything inside that scrolls on its own, such as an open
        task's table in the list, never do.
